# The line ending is part of the format.
#
# `index.jsonl`, the generated `SUMMARY.md` and every conformance golden are
# compared literally, and both engines write them with `\n`. A checkout that
# rewrote them to CRLF would leave the working tree permanently disagreeing
# with what the engine produces: the first verb would rewrite the whole file
# back to LF, and every commit would show it as wholly changed. The Windows
# CI job found this by failing the byte-for-byte round-trip over this repo's
# own tracker.
#
# So: normalise to LF in the object database, and check out LF everywhere,
# whatever `core.autocrlf` says on the machine doing the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
